---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import MainView from "../../layouts/MainView.astro";
import NavigationBar from "../../components/NavigationBar.astro";
import Chapter from "../../components/writing/Chapter.astro";
import Section from "../../components/writing/Section.astro";
import Link from "../../components/writing/Link.astro";
import Paragraph from "../../components/writing/Paragraph.astro";
import AboutTopic from "../../components/writing/AboutTopic.astro"
import InlineCode from "../../components/writing/InlineCode.astro"
---

<BaseLayout>
    <div class="flex flex-inital justify-center">
        <MainView>
            <NavigationBar />
            <Chapter>My Projects</Chapter>
            <Paragraph>
                Here I've listed many personal projects that I have worked on. Some
                projects are larger than others. And some doesn't lead to fully working
                "Applications".
            </Paragraph>

            <Section>Zinc, a Simple Image Processor</Section>
            <AboutTopic>
                Context, What it is, How to use it, Link.
            </AboutTopic>
            <Paragraph>
                <i>Zinc</i> is one of the first project I worked on. It is a simple
                program to manipulate/edit an image. The project is purely written in C.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                Zinc was a naïve attempt on creating an image processor as this project is
                quite broad and can be extended more and more to create a working
                production-grade software. My attempt contains only a handful of features.
                Such as: Grayscale Conversion, Brightness Adjustment, Tint, Color
                Inversion and more...
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                The program only works inside the command line through arguments passed to
                the program from the shell. The output image is written in the currently
                working directory(cwd).
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                    Here is the project on Github:{" "}
                    <Link
                        url="https://github.com/mubin-thinks/zinc"
                        anchorText="mubin-thinks/zinc"
                        external
                    />
            </Paragraph>

            <Section>OreoAdventures, a 2d Side Scrolling Game</Section>
            <AboutTopic>
                What it is, How it's played, Inspiration, Levels, Technical details, Link.
            </AboutTopic>
            <Paragraph>
                <i>OreoAdventures</i> is a small video game with a level system & gradual
                difficulty. The project was used to practice my Graphics Programming &
                Coding skills.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                The game is 2d and played only on a computer, The player is represented
                as a flying entity whose task is to collect all coins in a given level to
                unlock the door to the next level at the end. It must be done quick as
                their is a time limit. If the player looses any level, he will restart at
                Level 1.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                The flying entity, Coins & Environment Textures are inspired by Flappy
                Bird, Super Mario & Minecraft respectively.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                Their are 5 levels in the game with gradual difficulty, length and time
                limit. All levels imitate texture of the earth & the sky. Though much of
                the textures can be pollished.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                The game is written in C++ & OpenGL. The game was used to practice my
                coding skills and thus the code-base isn't organized well nor does it
                follow common coding-practices in terms of code structure.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                The Levels of the game is represented as a text-grid saved in{" "}
                <InlineCode>levels/</InlineCode> directory and loaded with{" "}
                <Link
                    url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Run-length_encoding"
                    anchorText="RLE(Run Length Encoding)"
                    external
                /> to save some memory.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                    Here is the project on Github:{" "}
                    <Link
                        url="https://github.com/mubin-thinks/oreoadventures"
                        anchorText="mubin-thinks/oreoadventures"
                        external
                    />
            </Paragraph>

            <Section>
                c-k-and-r-solutions, Solutions to The C Programming Language Book
            </Section>
            <AboutTopic>
                What it is, How to use it, Link.
            </AboutTopic>
            <Paragraph>
                This repository stores solutions of exercises in "The C Programming
                Language by Brian Kernighan & Dennis Ritchie". Chapter 7 & 8 are in the
                todos and the last 3 problems in chapter 5 is out of my reach. I shall try
                to solve them later.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                Instructions on how to run the solutions on a local machine is provided
                in the Github Readme.
            </Paragraph>
            <Paragraph>
                    Here is the project on Github:{" "}
                    <Link
                        url="https://github.com/mubin-thinks/c-k-and-r-solutions"
                        anchorText="mubin-thinks/c-k-and-r-solutions"
                        external
                    />
            </Paragraph>
        </MainView>
    </div>
</BaseLayout>